    "summary": "Dark Star > High Time epic, debut Uncle John’s Band, organ‑rich late‑’69 set",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a fiery 30‑minute Dark Star that segues into High Time, plus the first live Uncle John’s Band with Tom Constanten’s prominent organ. Black Peter and Good Lovin’ are solid, and Jerry’s youthful voice shines throughout.",
    "review": "December 4, 1969 at Fillmore West captures a historic moment as the Dead transition from their psychedelic heyday toward the Working‑Man’s Dead era. The centerpiece is an almost‑30‑minute Dark Star that erupts into a soaring High Time, showcasing Garcia’s spooky Strat tone and a relentless, slugging bass from Phil Lesh. Tom Constanten’s organ sits front‑and‑center on every track, adding the early‑Dead texture that fans love, while Pigpen’s harmonica and occasional keyboard flourishes inject extra grit. The set also marks the debut of Uncle John’s Band with vocal harmonies that hint at the forthcoming studio version, and strong renditions of Black Peter and Good Lovin’ round out a performance that is both historically significant and musically thrilling.",
